1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Every robot program begins with one pattern:
input, Brain, output.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:13,000
The Check button is our input.
It tells the robot something happened.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:20,000
The VEX IQ Brain reads that input
and follows these blocks from top to bottom.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,000
First, the screen says PRESS CHECK.
This gives us a visual instruction before motion.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:33,000
When I press Check,
the waiting block becomes true.

6
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:40,000
The Brain changes the screen to GO,
then drives forward for 300 millimeters.

7
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,000
When movement finishes,
the final output appears: DONE.

8
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Input is what the robot detects.
The Brain runs the program.

9
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Output is what the robot
shows or does.

10
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:04,000
If we change 300 to 500 millimeters,
which part stays the same?

11
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:10,000
And which output changes?

12
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Download the English and Thai lesson materials
from our open repository.

13
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Input your logic, spark their world.
See you in the next log.
